      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14256222/assets/e0dcc6b882545aefb50462f7cc3d32a14ef5f8c0cbefe696895ad46857800489.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ to give $y=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$",
